      "title": "English",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "================================================================================\n🛠️ FLUX-FILL ADAPTIVE PRE-PROCESSOR | By neron5480922\n================================================================================\n\nThis micro-workflow perfectly adapts ANY input image (portrait or \nlandscape) to a specified resolution, for example 1024x1024 for \nvideo generators (MiniMax / LTX). \nFlux-Fill automatically outpaints the missing edges, while the custom unsharp \nmasking node sharpens contours.\n\nREQUIRED MODELS & DIRECTORIES:\n\n1. Diffusion Model (Flux Fill):\n   • Filename: flux1-fill-dev.safetensors\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/unet/\n   • Source: Search for \"flux1-fill-dev\" on Civitai or Hugging Face.\n\n2. CLIP Text Encoders:\n   • Filename 1: clip_l.safetensors\n   • Filename 2: t5xxl_fp16.safetensors (or fp8_e4m3fn for low VRAM)\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/clip/\n\n3. VAE Model:\n   • Filename: ae.safetensors (Official Flux VAE)\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/vae/\n\nHOW TO USE IT:\n1. Load your raw photo into the \"Load Image\" node.\n2. Set target_width and target_height to your desired size (e.g., 1024).\n3. In the text field (inside the generator subgraph), you can type 2-3 words \n   describing the background to outpaint (e.g., \"living room, apartment interior\").\n4. Click Queue Prompt. get a picture !\n================================================================================\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "================================================================================\n🛠️ FLUX-FILL ADAPTIVE PRE-PROCESSOR | By neron5480922\n================================================================================\n\nThis micro-workflow perfectly adapts ANY input image (portrait or \nlandscape) to a specified resolution, for example 1024x1024 for \nvideo generators (MiniMax / LTX). \nFlux-Fill automatically outpaints the missing edges, while the custom unsharp \nmasking node sharpens contours.\n\nREQUIRED MODELS & DIRECTORIES:\n\n1. Diffusion Model (Flux Fill):\n   • Filename: flux1-fill-dev.safetensors\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/unet/\n   • Source: Search for \"flux1-fill-dev\" on Civitai or Hugging Face.\n\n2. CLIP Text Encoders:\n   • Filename 1: clip_l.safetensors\n   • Filename 2: t5xxl_fp16.safetensors (or fp8_e4m3fn for low VRAM)\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/clip/\n\n3. VAE Model:\n   • Filename: ae.safetensors (Official Flux VAE)\n   • Directory: ComfyUI/models/vae/\n\nHOW TO USE IT:\n1. Load your raw photo into the \"Load Image\" node.\n2. Set target_width and target_height to your desired size (e.g., 1024).\n3. In the text field (inside the generator subgraph), you can type 2-3 words \n   describing the background to outpaint (e.g., \"living room, apartment interior\").\n4. Click Queue Prompt. get a picture !\n================================================================================\n"
      },
